For Euler–Bernoulli flexural waves:
\[
\omega = \sqrt{\frac{EI}{\rho A}} k^2
\]
For a rectangular section bending about its neutral axis,
\[
\frac{I}{A}=\frac{h^2}{12}
\]
with \(h=0.010\ \text{m}\). Thus
\[
\alpha=\sqrt{\frac{EI}{\rho A}}
=h\sqrt{\frac{E}{12\rho}}
=0.010\sqrt{\frac{200\times10^9}{12(7850)}}
\approx 14.571\ \text{m}^2/\text{s}
\]
At \(f=1\ \text{kHz}\), \(\omega=2\pi f=6283.185\ \text{rad/s}\), so
\[
c_g=\frac{d\omega}{dk}=2\sqrt{\alpha\omega}
\approx 2\sqrt{14.571(6283.185)}
\approx 605.15\ \text{m/s}
\]

FINAL ANSWER: 605.15 m/s
CONFIDENCE: 99
